Sogen: a running process's exit status is STILL_ACTIVE

ProcessBasicInformation on the process asking left its ExitStatus 0,
which GetExitCodeProcess hands back as the exit code: the process read
itself as one that had exited with 0. A running process's is
STATUS_PENDING, STILL_ACTIVE to GetExitCodeProcess, as Sogen already
answers for its child processes and the synthetic ones it vouches for.

nodecode's pid-live-p opens a process for query and asks its exit code;
asked about its own pid, under Sogen it answered no.

diff --git a/src/windows-emulator/syscalls/process.cpp b/src/windows-emulator/syscalls/process.cpp
index 6b1c67e..b9e6bcd 100644
--- a/src/windows-emulator/syscalls/process.cpp
+++ b/src/windows-emulator/syscalls/process.cpp
@@ -680,6 +680,7 @@ namespace sogen
                         c.proc.kusd.access([](const KUSER_SHARED_DATA64& kusd) { return kusd.ActiveProcessorCount; });
                     basic_info.AffinityMask = processor_count >= 64 ? ~0ull : ((1ull << processor_count) - 1);
                     basic_info.UniqueProcessId = c.proc.process_id;
+                    basic_info.ExitStatus = STATUS_PENDING; // STILL_ACTIVE: the process asking is running
                 };
 
                 switch (process_information_length)
